      "text": [
        " عَيْنَيْهِ اَلْمَاءُ فَيُنْتَزَعُ اَلْمَاءُ مِنْهَا فَيَسْتَلْقِي عَلَى ظَهْرِهِ اَلْأَيَّامَ اَلْكَثِيرَةَ أَرْبَعِينَ يَوْماً أَوْ أَقَلَّ أَوْ أَكْثَرَ فَيَمْتَنِعُ مِنَ اَلصَّلاَةِ إِلاَّ إِيمَاءً وَ هُوَ عَلَى حَالِهِ فَقَالَ «لاَ بَأْسَ بِذَلِكَ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1035 - Samahat ibn Mehran asked about a man who has an eye condition (cataracts or similar) and undergoes a procedure to remove the issue, requiring him to lie on his back for many days—forty days, or possibly fewer or more. As a result, he can only perform his prayers by gestures due to his condition.\nThe response was: \"There is no harm in that.\""
        ]
      }
    },
